<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert William Wilcox</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1855">1855</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert William Wilcox was a Native Hawaiian soldier and politician who led armed risings in 1889 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayonet-constitution">Bayonet Constitution</a> and in January 1895 against the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, aiming to restore Queen Liliʻuokalani. Trained at a military academy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, he was sentenced to death after the 1895 rising, but the sentence was commuted. In 1900 he was elected Hawaii's first delegate to the US Congress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-william-wilcox.jpg" alt="Robert William Wilcox" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_William_Wilcox_1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
